[Act 12 of 2024 wef 30/08/2024]
(5) For the purposes of this section and section 150C, a reference to a foreign regulatory authority is a reference to an authority of a country or jurisdiction other than Singapore, exercising any function that corresponds to a regulatory function of the Authority under the Monetary Authority of Singapore Act 1970 or any of the written laws set out in the Schedule to that Act.
[2/2009]
